!
! WHAT WAS HANDED TO strap_asm EXACTLY AS PRINTED, and taken:
! ALL THIRTY-NINE COMPILING STATEMENTS.  Nothing was dropped and no
! row was left failing.  THE DECK REPRODUCES ALL FORTY-SIX PRINTED
! HALF WORDS CHARACTER FOR CHARACTER ON THE FIRST ASSEMBLY.  No
! assembler limitation was hit.  The only editorial changes are the
! ones the deck format requires -- blanks removed from names, which
! the page itself licenses by printing "S FILEK" on line 24 and
! "S FILE K" on line 40 -- and the ONE labelled substitution above,
! line 4's "SLC,$" written as a hard origin.
!
! TWO THINGS WORTH SAYING ABOUT WHAT ASSEMBLED FIRST TRY, because
! both were briefed as recent repairs and both are exercised here:
!
!   * line 34's "CTL,0.0($14),0.0" is a CONTROL CODE WRITTEN AS AN
!     ADDRESS and compiles word-granular, printing 000000.00 8E
!     000000.05 00.
!   * line 45's "BZB,$5.24,K SP TM" names INDEX REGISTER 5 BY ITS
!     STORAGE WORD: $5 resolves to word 0o25 and the row prints
!     000025.30 80.  Written "$5.24" exactly as printed.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT COULD NOT BE RESOLVED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (a) "R10"'s SECOND GLYPH.  See GLYPHS (4).  It prints as an open
!     round glyph; the page's own letter O (CNOP, line 31) prints
!     closed and the page's own proven digit zeros (lines 32, 33,
!     34) print open, which is why the deck writes R10 -- but
!     docs/transcription_workflow.md says openness is not a reliable
!     O/0 test, the name is referenced only on this page, and
!     listing_oracle never checks spellings.  IF THIS NAME IS WRONG,
!     NOTHING IN THIS REPOSITORY CAN SAY SO.  The cheapest thing
!     that would: a page that branches to 220140.00 from outside.
!     None was found -- and NOTHING OUTSIDE THIS PAGE NAMES ANY OF
!     THE FOUR.  Both volume OCRs were grepped for the half words
!     220120.40/.50, 220124.10, 220135.70 and 220140.00/.40 and the
!     only hits are this page's own rows (lines 8, 10 and 30).  So
!     the SPACE pseudo-op's own entry point R 1 has no located
!     caller anywhere in docs/ocr/, which is itself worth someone's
!     attention: the dispatch into it is on a page that either has
!     not been OCR'd legibly or reaches it by some other name.
!
! (b) THE BIT OFFSETS OF FIVE EXTERNALS ARE NOT READ HERE.
!     S FILEK (.38), S EVL MK (.32), S INST D (.0), S TIC (.0) and
!     S IO INS (.0) are all reached by INDEX instructions, whose
!     printed field spends bits 19-23 on the register.  Their
!     offsets come from printed pp.99, 101 and 108 and from the
!     repository's convention, NOT from this page.  The same holds
!     below bit 18 for every branch target: R MASK, R VFY, K SUPP,
!     M IOREJ, K N SYST, K SP TM, Z STEVL, K K LOC, K ILEGL and
!     K DENST are pinned by this page only to the HALF WORD.
!
! (c) THE LOCATION-COLUMN ASTERISK, lines 4, 26 and 48, confirmed at
!     900 dpi (line 4 in the BINARY-OUTPUT render, lines 26 and 48
!     in a LINE+LOCATION render).  Recorded, not explained.  NO RULE
!     IS PROPOSED FROM THIS PAGE: the three rows are an SLC, a
!     full-word BB in the middle of a routine, and the page's last
!     half-word branch, which have nothing in common.  Note that
!     this page would KILL the "every printed SLC,$ row carries it"
!     hypothesis only if it disagreed -- line 4 agrees with it, so
!     this page is NOT the discriminating case for that guess and
!     printed p.151 line 4 remains the one that refuted it.
!
! (d) "K N SYST" and "K SP TM" ARE SPELLED OFF THIS PAGE'S INK
!     ALONE.  No landed deck carries either name, and their only
!     other appearance is the volume OCR of printed p.163, which is
!     the same drum read worse.  Both addresses, though, are
!     corroborated by that OCR's LABEL ROWS (220174.40 and
!     220156.40), so the NAMES are the exposed part, not the
!     addresses.  printed p.163's transcriber will read both label
!     rows first hand and should compare.
!
! (e) "V-I" ON LINE 12 -- the mnemonic reads cleanly, assembles, and
!     prints the page's own 000000.45 0D, so it is settled; but this
!     deck did NOT find a primary-source page citation for the
!     operation's semantics and does not claim one.  The bits are
!     transcribed, not interpreted.
!
! (f) R MASK's DEFINING PAGE IS NOT PINNED.  See the external note.
!     The address is corroborated by the volume OCR's defining card;
!     the printed page number is not, because the headers between
!     volume-OCR lines 9130 and 9380 did not OCR.
!
! (g) WHAT CARD IH000041 IS.  See the serial note above.  It is
!     printed on neither printed p.162 nor printed p.163 -- both
!     read at 900 dpi -- and nothing in the address chain is missing
!     because of it.  No explanation is offered beyond "it is not a
!     lost instruction", which the contiguous counter proves.  The
!     cheapest thing that would settle it: whether any other
!     p.162/p.163-style page break in this volume also skips exactly
!     one serial.  That is a question about the VOLUME, not about
!     this page, and this deck does not answer it.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE JOIN BACKWARD -- printed p.161
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 4's printed "SLC,$" at 220120.40 IS the counter arriving from
! p.161, and the volume OCR of p.161 (an index of another page)
! shows a half word at 220120.00 as that page's last located row,
! which leaves exactly 220120.40.  p.161's transcriber should find
! their last row at 220120.00 and their own SLC near 220115.00.
! WORTH FLAGGING: p.161's OCR lines 24-26 are "SV,2,S TIC",
! "KVI,4,4.0" and "BZXE,K ILEGL" -- byte for byte this page's lines
! 14, 15 and 16.  The two pages print the same three cards, which is
! a free cross-check on both once p.161 lands.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE JOIN FORWARD -- a falsifiable prediction for printed p.163
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 48 is a half-word branch at 220147.00, so THE COUNTER LEAVES
! THIS PAGE AT 220147.40.  Four ways to break that claim:
!
!   1. printed p.163's first LOCATED row should be 220147.40.
!   2. Its heading-row LOCATION field should read 220147 -- NOT
!      blank -- because its line 1 is a located instruction and not
!      a banner.  A blank there would be a refutation.
!   3. Its line 1 should be "SIC,K K IND", with its half-word
!      branch "B,K IO IND" as line 2 at 220150.00: a SIC/branch pair
!      straddling nothing, both on p.163.
!   4. p.163 should carry K SP TM's label row at 220156.40 and
!      K N SYST's at 220174.40, which this page's lines 45 and 43
!      reach.
!
! (1) and (4) are this page's own arithmetic and ink.  (3) and the
! exact wording come from the volume OCR of PDF p.170, which is an
! INDEX and not a witness; p.163's own render decides it.
!
! >>> ALL FOUR WERE CONFIRMED WHILE THIS DECK WAS BEING WRITTEN. <<<
! printed pp.161 and 163 are being transcribed in the same batch, and
! their decks (not yet landed in the repository at the time of
! writing) report, each off its OWN page's ink:
!
!   p.161  its last line, line 28, is "220120.00  220017.50 00
!          B,W 23K  -FAKE EOP" -- a HALF WORD at 220120.00, leaving
!          the counter at 220120.40, which is this page's printed
!          "SLC,$".  Its card serials are IG0000nn, which is why this
!          page's are IH000001 onward.
!   p.163  its line 1 is "220147.40  221371.00 80  SIC,K K IND" and
!          its line 2 "220150.00  221370.10 00  B,K IO IND"; its
!          heading-row LOCATION field reads 220147; and it DEFINES
!          K SP TM at 220156.40 and K N SYST at 220174.40 -- both
!          exactly as SYNed here.
!
! Those are readings of DIFFERENT PAGES by different transcribers, so
! they are admissible under docs/transcription_workflow.md rule 5 in
! a way the volume OCR is not.  They are recorded as corroboration,
! not as the source: every number above was derived from this page
! before they were consulted.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------

!SYM   R1       220120.40
!SYM   R2       220124.00
!SYM   R9SKP    220135.40
!SYM   R10      220140.00
!SYM   RS1FLK   220143.00
!CHECK 220120.40 | 000076.01 01 | line 5 R 1 LVI,$0,62.0 -- 62 decimal is word 0o76; the register field .01 is $0
!CHECK 220121.00 | 220124.10 00 | line 6 B,R 2 -- forward reference to line 12, internal to this page; bit 18 clear is R 2's .00
!CHECK 220121.40 | 000176.01 01 | line 7 LVI,$0,126.0 -- 126 decimal is 0o176, the same card as line 5 with one operand changed
!CHECK 220122.00 | 220124.10 00 | line 8 B,R 2 -- byte for byte line 6's word, printed a second time
!CHECK 220122.40 | 000077.01 01 | line 9 LVI,$0,63.0 -- 0o77; the third printing of this card, and the one whose "$0" prints closed
!CHECK 220123.00 | 220124.10 00 | line 10 B,R 2 -- the third identical branch; three printings of one word is a free check on R 2
!CHECK 220123.40 | 000177.01 01 | line 11 LVI,$0,127.0 -- 0o177, the fourth control code, the only one with no comment
!CHECK 220124.00 | 000000.45 0D | line 12 R 2 V-I,2,.32 -- the .45 is bit 18 (the .32 operand) plus register 2; the byte 0D prints with an open round glyph and is settled by what produced it
!CHECK 220124.40 | 000000.32 8A 001000.36 F0 | line 13 CM1111(BU,1),S CH OP($10) -- a VFL operand prints its FULL address, so 0o32 = bit 26 of S CH OP is checked; low nibble A is index $10; 001000.36 is connective 1111
!CHECK 220125.40 | 215265.05 30 | line 14 SV,2,S TIC -- index instruction: .05 is register 2 and bit 18 is clear, so only S TIC's word is checked
!CHECK 220126.00 | 000004.11 04 | line 15 KVI,4,4.0 -- byte for byte printed p.161 line 25's card (volume OCR, index)
!CHECK 220126.40 | 220064.32 C0 | line 16 BZXE,K ILEGL -- byte for byte the word printed p.159 line 6 prints and the word printed p.161 line 26 prints; bit 18 clear checks K ILEGL's .00 against p.160's own label row
!CHECK 220127.00 | 221153.07 01 | line 17 LVI,3,R MASK -- .07 is register 3 against line 36's .03 for register 1; bit 18 clear checks R MASK's half word
!CHECK 220127.40 | 000005.41 3C | line 18 SV,0,S CTL OP($12) -- .41 is bit 18 set plus register 0; compare line 29's .42 for register 1 on the SAME operand, which is what shows the field carries the register
!CHECK 220130.00 | 000002.47 3C | line 19 SV,$3,S EVL MK($12) -- register 3 on an SV prints .47 where line 17's LVI register 3 prints .07; bit 18 set is S EVL MK's .32
!CHECK 220130.40 | 000002.00 8C | line 20 SIC,S EVL TB($12) -- a SIC prints the bare 24-bit address, so all six octal digits of S EVL TB's offset are checked
!CHECK 220131.00 | 221144.50 00 | line 21 B,Z STEVL -- same card as line 20; bit 18 set checks Z STEVL's .40 against printed p.160's render
!CHECK 220131.40 | 220065.50 00 | line 22 B,KKLOC -- bit 18 set checks K K LOC's .40, printed p.160's own label row
!CHECK 220132.00 | 221161.10 00 | line 23 B,R VFY -- bit 18 clear; R VFY's own label row is at 221161.00 later in the volume
!CHECK 220132.40 | 000007.52 3C | line 24 LV,5,S FILEK($12) -- .52 is bit 18 set plus register 5; this is the LV/SV discriminator against line 18's .41 (bit 23)
!CHECK 220133.00 | 220135.71 C2 | line 25 BXVGZ,R 9 SKP -- forward reference to line 29, internal; bit 18 set is R 9 SKP's .40, and BXVCZ/BXVOZ are not instructions
!CHECK 220133.40 | 000005.53 8C 220064.34 02 | line 26 BB,S CTL OP+.1($12),K ILEGL -- a BB operand prints its FULL bit address, so 0o53 = 43 = S CTL OP's 42 plus one bit, which pins p.101's offset exactly; the second group's bit 18 is clear, K ILEGL's .00 again (this LOCATION carries the second asterisk)
!CHECK 220134.40 | 000006.00 8C | line 27 SIC,S SCR PM($12) -- a SIC, so all six octal digits of S SCR PM's 6.0 are checked
!CHECK 220135.00 | 220143.10 00 | line 28 B,RS1 FLK -- same card as line 27; forward reference to line 43, internal to this page, and byte for byte printed p.151 line 37's word
!CHECK 220135.40 | 000005.42 3C | line 29 R 9 SKP LV,$1,S CTL OP($12) -- .42 against line 18's .41 on the same operand: bit 23 is the LV/SV bit and bits 19-22 the register
!CHECK 220136.00 | 220140.43 D0 | line 30 SVA,1,R10.32 -- forward reference to line 34 plus 32 bits; bit 18 set is the +.32, and D0 is the SVA byte against line 18's 3C for SV
!CHECK 220136.40 | 000000.30 00 | line 31 CNOP -- the page's only CNOP, and the row whose letter O is the closed-glyph reference for R10
!CHECK 220137.00 | 220140.00 10 | line 32 LX,0,$+1.0 -- $ is 220137.00 so the target is 220140.00, which is R10; this row checks the deck's own counter and reaches line 34 by arithmetic rather than by name
!CHECK 220137.40 | 000004.01 1C | line 33 SX,0,S IO INS($12) -- same card as line 32; byte 1C against line 32's 10 is the LX/SX pair, as .01 against .00 is bit 23
!CHECK 220140.00 | 000000.00 8E 000000.05 00 | line 34 R10 CTL,0.0($14),0.0 -- a control code written as an ADDRESS, word-granular; low nibble E is index $14
!CHECK 220141.00 | 000000.74 8B 001000.36 F0 | line 35 CM1111(BU,1),S CTL($11) -- a VFL operand prints its FULL address: 0o74 = bit 60 of S CTL, checked exactly; low nibble B is index $11
!CHECK 220142.00 | 216242.03 01 | line 36 LVI,1,K SUPP -- .03 is register 1; bit 18 clear checks K SUPP's half word as nineteen other decks write it
!CHECK 220142.40 | 221261.10 00 | line 37 B,M IOREJ -- same card as line 36; bit 18 clear
!CHECK 220143.00 | 000007.31 8C 220174.74 00 | line 43 RS1 FLK BZB,S SYSTM($12),K N SYST -- 0o31 = bit 25 pins S SYSTM exactly; the second group's bit 18 is SET, which is this page's reading of K N SYST's .40
!CHECK 220144.00 | 000000.74 8B 001000.36 F0 | line 44 CM1111(BU,1),S CTL($11) -- byte for byte line 35's card, printed a second time on this page
!CHECK 220145.00 | 000025.30 80 220156.74 00 | line 45 BZB,$5.24,K SP TM -- $5 is index register 5's storage word 0o25 and .24 decimal is 0o30, so the first group checks the register-word convention; bit 18 set is K SP TM's .40
!CHECK 220146.00 | 000000.01 01 | line 46 LVI,0,S INST D -- register 0 prints .01 exactly as line 5's "$0" does, which is what shows $0 and 0 are one register
!CHECK 220146.40 | 000005.00 8C | line 47 SIC,S RET AD($12) -- a SIC, so all six octal digits of S RET AD's 5.0 are checked
!CHECK 220147.00 | 217674.50 00 | line 48 B,K DENST -- same card as line 47; bit 18 SET checks K DENST's .40, and the counter leaves this page at 220147.40 (this LOCATION carries the second asterisk)
